WEBVTT

NOTE
English narration for the career showreel.

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.497
I am Beni Kun.

2
00:00:01.502 --> 00:00:02.674
Here is the work.

3
00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:11.808
The focus is end-to-end automation,
reporting, and CI for a multi-region SaaS

4
00:00:11.808 --> 00:00:12.458
platform.

5
00:00:12.463 --> 00:00:16.651
I keep the checks, the reports, and the
pipeline in one system.

6
00:00:16.656 --> 00:00:18.126
That is the current role.

7
00:00:20.248 --> 00:00:24.575
The core is Python 3.13, pytest, and
Playwright.

8
00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:31.796
I also use xdist, JUnit, GitLab CI,
Kubernetes, S3, CloudFront, and Slack.

9
00:00:32.249 --> 00:00:36.015
JUnit XML becomes a per-run HTML report.

10
00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:39.023
Publishing goes through S3 behind
CloudFront.

11
00:00:39.028 --> 00:00:40.584
Slack carries the link.

12
00:00:40.589 --> 00:00:46.159
The dashboard keeps pass rate, a daily
timeline, an environment matrix, and a

13
00:00:46.159 --> 00:00:46.955
flaky list.

14
00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:49.988
Flaky versus broken comes from run
history.

15
00:00:49.993 --> 00:00:51.783
Numbers shown are sample data.

16
00:00:52.248 --> 00:00:54.944
A test calls a page wrapper, then
Playwright.

17
00:00:54.949 --> 00:00:58.325
Workers share one logged-in session under
a file lock.

18
00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:02.226
A scarce test-data pool is allocated and
released under a lock.

19
00:01:02.231 --> 00:01:05.785
Logs, artifacts, and teardown stay on the
test.

20
00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:08.721
A headed run on the public practice shop.

21
00:01:08.726 --> 00:01:11.468
Search, then filter, add to cart.

22
00:01:11.473 --> 00:01:13.192
The public sample passed.

23
00:01:16.249 --> 00:01:22.468
With Chrome DevTools MCP I inspect, choose
locators, scaffold the test, run a check,

24
00:01:22.468 --> 00:01:23.652
and self-review.

25
00:01:23.657 --> 00:01:25.790
Sanity jobs keep artifacts.

26
00:01:26.248 --> 00:01:29.797
Appeals, driver client, flakes, this
pipeline.
